# config/skill-sync-exclude - rsync --exclude patterns for the remote
# secondmate skill sync (bin/fm-remote-skill-sync.sh). Copy this into a local,
# gitignored config/skill-sync-exclude and edit. One pattern per non-empty,
# non-comment line. Presence fully replaces the script's built-in default set
# below, it does not merge with it.
#
# no-mistakes is excluded because a remote host installs it itself; overwriting
# it with the local copy could break a working install. notebooklm is a large
# local data cache. skill-creator, notebooklm-to-skill, and
# notebooklm-to-skill-workspace are authoring tools a worker host does not run.
# The rest is ordinary build residue.
notebooklm/
notebooklm-to-skill/
notebooklm-to-skill-workspace/
skill-creator/
no-mistakes/
__pycache__
.venv
node_modules
